sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-pa02-12> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Animals with strong and solid bones, such as the lion, have hardly any marrow, the lion's being so insignificant that its bones look as though they had none.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The lion's bones have almost no marrow";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, On the Parts of Animals (De Partibus Animalium), Book II, Part 6; translated by William Ogle, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: lion (Panthera leo) and other animals with strong compact bones"
}
